From 84103ec6fb740251c6b60cdea3828c1cb94bd6ce Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: USA-RedDragon <USA-RedDragon@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 15 Nov 2026 02:52:37 -0600
Subject: [PATCH] fix(approval): a Code from External card offers to allow its
 source for the chat

A smart approval card for outside code now offers "Allow code from <source> in this chat" for downloads and installs as well as clones, and for a subagent's card. The choice records a chat grant that covers later commands of the chat and its subagents that run code from the same source.

Before, only a git clone of a session path gave the card a source: a curl or wget download (-o, -O, a release asset) and pip, npm, go or cargo installs from a URL had none, so the card offered once and deny only, and the Telegram card never rendered the choice. Now the source comes from the fetch URL or from the URLs the command names (github.com/owner/repo for clones, release assets, raw and codeload URLs; host plus project for package hosts; the host otherwise). Parsing reads the host, so look-alike hosts and userinfo tricks are other sources. A grant covers a command only when every fetched path it runs in and every remote source it names is granted, and no dangerous pattern but chmod +x then run matches; a pipe to a shell, another repo or a bare registry package is not covered. Telegram renders the choice as a button row of its own.
